Sval: browser-chrome fails a stalled test, not a long one

Tester's time limit already tells a hang from a long test: when the limit
passes, a test that logged a result or message in the last half of it is
let run on (up to MAX_UNEXPECTED_TIMEOUTS more limits), and only a quiet
one fails as "Test timed out". A long test that then passed still failed
at its end with "This test exceeded the timeout threshold", so a test's
length, which a runner's load decides, failed a run whose every check
passed. The end-of-test failure becomes a log line; the stall check stays.

